  [#D7D7AF]release.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Adopt the release and carry close history through Python [/bold #D7AFFF]     [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]storage[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]core-adopt[dim] · [dim][/dim]after core-model[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]core-adopt: raise the sase-core-rs window to the release from core-model[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and thread close_history through the Python model, wire conversion, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]issues.jsonl, the SQLite mirror with its migration, and the projection [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]repair guard.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Shared reopen presentation vocabulary[/bold #D7AFFF]                         [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]presentation[dim] · [dim][/dim]after core-adopt[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]presentation: add sase/bead/reopen_presentation.py with the accent, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]glyph, section label, badge, record labels, search text, and the single [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]shared join that decides which +1 entry reopened a bead.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]sase bead show, JSON, list badges, and search[/bold #D7AFFF]                 [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]cli[dim] · [dim][/dim]after presentation[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]cli: render the PREVIOUSLY CLOSED section and the reopening-+1 marker in[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]bead detail, emit close_history in detail JSON, add the reopen badge to [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]list/ready/search rows, and make archived close reasons searchable.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Prior-close warning in the TaskTriage gate[/bold #D7AFFF]                    